e": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's backgrounds in a wider variety  of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Verb + -ing and to + verb", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A gerund works like a noun. It is made by adding \"-ing\" to the base form of a verb. You can use a gerund as the subject or the object of a sentence, or as the complement.<br/>The infinitive is the base form of a verb - \u201cto + verb\u201d.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A gerund is the -ing form of a verb that acts as a noun. The noun refers to an activity instead of a person or thing. You can use a gerund as the subject, the complement, or the object of a sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/><br/>  Subject of sentence:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Traveling in the winter is very cold!</span><br/><br/>  Complement of sentence:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">My favorite hobbies are swimming and jogging.</span><br/><br/>  Object of sentence:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm excited to start working in your restaurant.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An infinitive is a verb form that can act as a noun. It is formed with to + base form of the verb. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">to talk</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to enjoy</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to play</span><br/> You can<span class=\"italic\">not</span> add <span class=\"strong\">s</span>, <span class=\"strong\">es</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ed</span>, or <span class=\"strong\">ing</span> to the end. It is not a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I wanted <span class=\"strong\">to know</span>  what kind of adjustments I would need <span class=\"strong\">to make</span> to my life here.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A phrasal verb is made up of a verb and one or more prepositions, or particles. They are very common, particularly in informal spoken English. Adding a preposition to a verb often completely changes the meaning that the original verb has on its own. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Phrasal verbs can be separable or inseparable. <br> Separable phrasal verbs take an object between the verb and the preposition. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inseparable phrasal verbs are very common. The verb and preposition must stay together. The object cannot come after the verb.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  Examples: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">When do you get up during the week?</span></li> <li>take off = leave the ground  <br/> The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out!  You're going to hurt yourself doing that!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to read up on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to read information about a subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to keep at\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to continue doing something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to carry on with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to continue doing something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to make up for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to compensate for something missing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to see to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to take care of something\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I read up on Boston's winters to prepare myself! <br/>           <span class=\"strong\">  Bob</span>:  Our summers make up for the cold, though. You'll see.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to read up on", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time researching information on something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I read up on Boston's winters to prepare myself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use in a new work environment.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to keep at", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to continue to do something; to persevere", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: You need to understand how the kitchen works before you start working.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I'll keep at it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to carry on with ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to continue doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need to carry on with today's tasks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make up for", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to compensate for something missing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our summers make up for the cold winters.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to see to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to deal with or take responsibility for someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need to see to my customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "work ethic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a belief in the importance of work to build character", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You seem to have a strong work ethic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "adjustment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to adapt to a situation or condition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wanted to know what kind of adjustments I would need to make to my life here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a list of five places you have been in the last few days.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange the list with a partner. Ask and answer the question <span class=\"italic\">Why did you go to ... ?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use infinitives to give your answer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now, write five sentences about yourself using a gerund.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use adjectives to complete the sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange with a partner and discuss.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a list of places I have been to lately.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask and answer questions bout the places.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences using gerunds.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss the sentences with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}